---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'About Eternal Heart | Cameron Gaut';
const description =
  'Learn the story behind Eternal Heart, the ambient and healing music project of Cameron Gaut in Kauaʻi.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />
  <main class="page-main">
    <section class="section section--sm page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">About Eternal Heart</span>
        <h1 class="section-title">Music rooted in <em>presence</em>.</h1>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="section-body">
          Eternal Heart is the artist project of Cameron Gaut, a bansuri flute player,
          producer, and sound facilitator based in Kauaʻi, Hawaiʻi.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section page-section">
      <div class="container about-bio">
        <div class="about-bio__image-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/cameron-gaut-eternal-heart.avif"
            alt="Cameron Gaut — Eternal Heart"
            class="about-bio__image"
            width="600"
            height="750"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="about-bio__text">
          <article class="card page-card">
            <h2>Artist Story</h2>
            <p>
              Cameron's relationship with music began as a teenager, spending hours at his laptop
              experimenting with Propellerhead Reason and FL Studio — taught the basics by his older
              brother, then quickly self-directed. While his peers were playing video games, he was
              learning how sound could be shaped from scratch.
            </p>
            <p>
              Around the same time, living with his mother and her partner — who was part Native
              American — he discovered a collection of Native flutes in the house. He picked one
              up, fell in love with its resonance and organic ease, and never put it down. On his
              eighteenth birthday, his mother gave him his own.
            </p>
            <p>
              In his early twenties, a deep immersion in the music of Shpongle — the British
              psychedelic ambient duo whose sound wove silver flute melodies through electronic
              atmospheres — opened a new direction. Wanting to recreate that quality, Cameron
              began teaching himself silver flute. Formal lessons didn't take. Self-study did.
            </p>
            <p>
              The pivotal moment came in 2017 at a concert in Portland, Oregon, where he saw
              master bansuri flutist Steve Gorn perform alongside Benjy Wertheimer on esraj.
              The sound stopped him completely. He had loved Indian classical music since high
              school, but hearing the bansuri live — the breath behind every phrase, the way
              each note bent and dissolved — was something different entirely. He approached
              Gorn after the show, asked where to find a flute, and was offered lessons on
              the spot. He accepted.
            </p>
            <p>
              Under Gorn's guidance, Cameron immersed himself in the raga tradition: its melodic
              frameworks, its relationship with time and season, its insistence that breath and
              presence are the instrument as much as the bamboo is. The practice reshaped not
              just his playing but his understanding of what music could do.
            </p>
            <p>
              In 2020, Cameron relocated with his wife and their young child from Oregon to Kauaʻi, Hawaiʻi.
              The island met him with
              an entirely new sonic world — ocean swell, dawn birdsong, rain moving through the
              canopy — and the impulse to build something new grew out of that landscape. His
              wife offered a guiding question: what name would capture how he wanted listeners to
              feel? The answer came quickly. <em>Eternal Heart</em> — a phrase that, to Cameron,
              speaks to the soul's continuity and the practice of living from the center of one's
              own being.
            </p>
            <p>
              The debut album, <em>Coming Home</em>, was recorded and ready before Cameron felt
              confident releasing it. A friend's involvement with the netlabel High Vibe Records
              opened a door; he submitted the album, they said yes, and the music found its
              audience. That first release gave him the confidence to keep going. He has been
              self-releasing music steadily ever since — each album and single a further
              exploration of the space where ambient electronics, bansuri flute, and the living
              sound of Kauaʻi converge.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card page-card">
            <h2>Core Influences</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Indian classical raga and bansuri flute traditions</li>
              <li>Electronic music and sound design</li>
              <li>Ambient and cinematic minimalism</li>
              <li>Mindfulness and somatic healing arts</li>
              <li>Nature field recordings and organic textures</li>
              <li>Bansuri flute traditions and breath-led phrasing</li>
              <li>Ambient and cinematic minimalism</li>
              <li>Mindfulness and somatic healing arts</li>
              <li>Nature field recordings and organic textures</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card page-card">
            <h2>Mission</h2>
            <p>
              To serve humanity with sound — to create music and experiences that support regulation, reflection, and inner
              connection. Every release and session is designed to help listeners return to a
              grounded, heart-centered state.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact">Work Together</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-main { padding-top: 90px; }
  .page-hero { padding-bottom: 44px; }
  .page-section { padding-top: 40px; }

  .about-bio {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 420px 1fr;
    gap: 52px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .about-bio__image-wrap {
    position: sticky;
    top: 110px;
  }
  .about-bio__image {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 16px;
    object-fit: cover;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    filter: saturate(0.9);
  }
  .about-bio__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
  }

  .page-card { padding: 30px; }
  .page-card h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .page-card p,
  .page-card li {
    color: var(--color-cream-dim);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .page-card p:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .page-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
  .page-card .btn { margin-top: 16px; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-bio {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
    .about-bio__image-wrap { position: static; }
    .about-bio__image { max-width: 340px; }
  }
</style>
